      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T15:04:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by unexpected behavior? Looks like the example you mentioned is just how we implemented AvbOps, like [extern \"C\" fn read_is_device_unlocked(..) -\u003e AvbIOResult](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/avb/src/ops.rs;l\u003d124;drc\u003d75d0563476ed6fa33238e10c22e0eac262b84ef4) where `AvbIOResult` is a generated enum.\n\nCurrently we have two versions of such code for several enums (DiceMode, DiceResult, DiceConfig). In the other lib (aosp/2411698), some names also got tweaked a bit. It\u0027s better to have just one type so that they won\u0027t diverge even more. I prefer not to create a new type / conversion for everything and copy-paste them in two places just because there\u0027s a prefix `k` in front of enum name.\n\nIn the long run, maybe we can extract a nostd version of the other lib `diced/open_dice_cbor` and re-used it here after simplifying both code.",
